# Settings-file keys a project of this type can never be registered with
# (issue #569), one per line: the key, a blank, then the reason shown to
# the user. register_project.sh refuses a key listed here, given with
# --set or set by a settings file kept from an earlier registration
# (--remove --keep-settings), before it writes anything. The key stays accepted by
# `project_setting.sh set` on a registered project (its removal is a line
# of docs/manifest/roadmap.md), where the adapter refuses it at use. Read
# by registration_refused_setting in .agent/scripts/_project_registry.sh;
# validate_adapter.sh checks every entry is a known key, listed once, with
# a reason.
source the manifest route it selected is removed, and the adapter refuses a root that sets it; a manifest in the new format is read from a root the manifest tool set up: register a new, empty directory from the manifest in one step, with no source, source_ref or source_path setting (register_project.sh <dir> --manifest <file> --distro <distro> [--role <role>], which runs the manifest tool's init in it; a URL source: docs/manifest/design.md, "A root that sets source")
source_ref it is read with source only, whose manifest route is removed; the adapter refuses a root that sets it: register a new, empty directory from the manifest in one step, with no source, source_ref or source_path setting (register_project.sh <dir> --manifest <file> --distro <distro> [--role <role>], which runs the manifest tool's init in it; a URL source: docs/manifest/design.md, "A root that sets source")
source_path it is read with source only, whose manifest route is removed; the adapter refuses a root that sets it: register a new, empty directory from the manifest in one step, with no source, source_ref or source_path setting (register_project.sh <dir> --manifest <file> --distro <distro> [--role <role>], which runs the manifest tool's init in it; a URL source: docs/manifest/design.md, "A root that sets source")
